in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @uuid
in @uuid/spectral
in @epistemologic/reality/time
in @epistemologic/property/content_addressed

# @uuid/spectral/time — the annotation-address species.
#
# Sub-species under @uuid/spectral. Composes the LANDED
# `uuid_spectral` identity (128 bits; @glass three-layer contract
# intact) with a trailing `@time/monotonic.instant` facet. The
# resulting carrier IS the substrate-decl form of annotation-address
# byte-comparison for R4 dispatch: argsort by hamming distance on the
# 48-bit ACTIVE prefix IS the tournament ordering. Zero @fate
# machinery required.
#
# Path-namespace: sub-species under @uuid/spectral. Sibling-of-family
# precedent: `@subject/visibility/sheaf` under `@subject/visibility`
# (Landing 4 R2 discharge; `shards/subject/visibility/sheaf.mirror`).
#
# === Alex 2026-07-16 verbatim ratification ===
#
# In-transcript exchange (annotation-address discovery):
#
#   Alex saw R4 was choosing between three dispatch policies for
#   annotation-tournament ordering. Alex noticed the annotation-
#   *address structure itself* could carry the affinity signal, so
#   the tournament becomes byte-comparison on the navigable bits.
#   Zero @fate infrastructure needed for the affinity computation.
#
#   "This is literally the addressation ground EVERYTHING stands on."
#
# The ratified shape (verbatim):
#
#   type uuid_spectral_time = {
#     identity: uuid_spectral,             // 128 bits; @glass
#                                          // three-layer contract intact
#     time:     @time/monotonic.instant,   // full precision; already
#                                          // used by @gestalt.annotation.
#                                          // timestamp + @spectral/
#                                          // signature.signature_beat.
#                                          // timestamp
#   }
#
# Byte layout when serialized:
#
#   [ ACTIVE 48 | DARK 80 | time N ]
#
# where identity (128 bits) preserves @glass shard.id contract and
# time trails as a facet.
#
# Semantics (verbatim):
#
#   1. Identity for content-address dedup = 128-bit uuid_spectral
#      prefix only. Storage layer dedups on prefix; two writes of
#      the same content collapse regardless of time. @mirror/store
#      unchanged.
#   2. Time is a facet, NOT part of identity. Trailing bytes; used
#      for tie-breakers + causal ordering; does NOT participate in
#      dedup.
#   3. ACTIVE (leading 48 bits) drives @resonance/@fate byte-
#      comparison — pure, unmodified; peer-coupling geometry
#      unchanged.
#   4. R4-(a) dispatch = argsort by byte-distance on ACTIVE. No new
#      machinery. Substrate-decl form of Kuramoto-Aumann convergence
#      at annotation altitude.
#
# Algedonic form: byte-distance on ACTIVE = pain/pleasure gradient
# at address altitude. `@cyberpunk/algedonic` composition surface
# (currently entropy-based per `bootstrap/src/algedonic.rs`) can
# compose over this for future extension. NOT this arc.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# Both fields of `uuid_spectral_time` LANDED. Grep-verified prior
# to authorship:
#
#   1. `@uuid/spectral` LANDED at `shards/uuid/spectral.mirror`
#      (2026-06-06 second tick; Mara). Carries the 48/128 golden-
#      ratio-adjacent split (48 ACTIVE quantized SpectralCoordinate<5>
#      + 80 DARK BLAKE3-truncated content hash; 48/128 ≈ 0.375 vs
#      1/φ² ≈ 0.382). Big-endian on ACTIVE: byte-wise sort IS
#      lexicographic sort over the navigable coordinate. Range
#      scans on the 48-bit space compose with byte-wise sort.
#      Semantic types `route_signal` + `identity_signal` compose
#      into the record. Realized at `prism/core/src/spectral_uuid.rs`.
#
#   2. `@time/monotonic.instant` LANDED at
#      `shards/epistemologic/reality/time.mirror:151` (the `instant`
#      type at line 89 + broader `monotonic` frame carriers). Full
#      precision u64 nanoseconds; ~584 years of range; matches
#      BEAM's `erlang:monotonic_time(:nanosecond)` native unit.
#      Already composed OVER by `@gestalt.annotation.timestamp`
#      (`shards/gestalt.mirror:~253`) + `@spectral/signature.
#      signature_beat.timestamp` (`shards/spectral/signature.mirror:
#      ~89`). This species lifts the composition edge those consumers
#      already implicitly carried.
#
# Zero UUIDv5 / UUIDv7 / timestamped-UUID precedent in the corpus
# (Taut scout task #172). This species IS the novel substrate
# addressation ground. RFC 9562 §6 (UUIDv7 semantics) is a
# structural cousin — trailing time bytes as tie-breaker, dedup on
# identity prefix — but the substrate carries neither the RFC's byte
# layout nor its clock discipline; the substrate carries
# `@time/monotonic.instant` (its own time carrier) folded as a
# facet over its own `uuid_spectral` (its own identity carrier).
# Delightfully-boring: the compiler already knew.
#
# The ~61st instance of [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]:
# every field, action, and bilateral below cites LANDED carriers.
#
# === Reed-recursive ancestry (why THIS mount as sub-species) ===
#
# R4 in `docs/specs/gestalt-as-song-unfolding.md` §10 asked which
# annotation-tournament dispatch policy to land: (a) @fate
# reader-corpus-affinity, (b) chronological monotone, or (c)
# reader-selects. Alex saw the annotation-*address* could carry the
# affinity signal by construction — one altitude up from the policy
# question. The tournament dissolves into byte-comparison on
# `active_prefix(uuid_spectral_time)`. No `@fate` machinery. No
# adjudication between (a) / (b) / (c).
#
# The dispatch-policy question is not answered; it is dissolved. R4
# becomes CLOSED, not "documented end-state." @resonance + @dance
# shard-mints (previously R4-gating per `docs/math/gestalt/README.md`
# §11.6 Landing Condition 0) DECOUPLE from R4 v0.1.0. They stay
# forward-promised at `@gestalt.p_ent` operator-altitude (n≥2 tori)
# per the Landing Condition, but no longer block R4.
#
# The R4-dissolution move IS the addressation ground the compiler
# already knew about. The species-decl below writes it down.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (substrate-decl):
#   @uuid                     — root prism; universal 128-bit
#                               identifier discipline; equals + parse
#                               + format at the root altitude
#   @uuid/spectral            — sub-prism; carries route_signal (48
#                               bits ACTIVE) + identity_signal (80
#                               bits DARK); monoidal(uuid_spectral)
#                               property; @glass shard.id contract
#   @epistemologic/reality/time
#                             — family; carries duration + monotonic
#                               + wall + instant + tick + snapshot;
#                               nanosecond precision; leap-second-free
#
# Consumers (compose over this species; landed in Deliverable 3):
#   shards/gestalt.mirror     — annotation.address: uuid_spectral_time
#   shards/spectral/signature.mirror
#                             — signature_beat address facet;
#                               Alex-adjudicable cascade shape
#
# Forward-composition surfaces (named, not imported):
#   @resonance                — inter-peer coupling operator (spec-
#                               landed; shard-mint forward-promised
#                               per @gestalt.p_ent Landing Condition 0
#                               — DECOUPLED from R4 v0.1.0 by this
#                               species)
#   @dance                    — Kuramoto phase-lock; spec-landed;
#                               shard-mint forward-promised at same
#                               Landing Condition
#   @cyberpunk/algedonic      — pain/pleasure gradient at address
#                               altitude; composition surface for
#                               byte-distance-on-ACTIVE (future arc)
#   @fate                     — tournament dispatch; dispatch policy
#                               (a) IS argsort by
#                               affinity_distance(a, H_R) at address
#                               altitude; no new machinery required
#
# === Related shards / specs ===
#
# - shards/uuid.mirror
#     (root prism; universal 128-bit identifier discipline)
# - shards/uuid/spectral.mirror
#     (sub-prism; 48 ACTIVE + 80 DARK; monoidal + content_addressed)
# - shards/epistemologic/reality/time.mirror
#     (@epistemologic/reality/time family; instant + monotonic + tick)
# - shards/gestalt.mirror
#     (consumer: annotation carrier composes over this species)
# - shards/spectral/signature.mirror
#     (consumer: signature_beat carries address facet)
# - docs/specs/gestalt-as-song-unfolding.md §10 R4
#     (the residue this species CLOSES by construction)
# - docs/math/gestalt/README.md §11.6 Landing Condition 0
#     (@resonance + @dance shard-mints — DECOUPLED from R4 by this
#      species; stay forward-promised for operator-altitude n≥2 tori)
# - docs/math/uuid/spectral-time.md
#     (companion math foundation; categorical-product proof +
#      Kuramoto-Aumann convergence formalization + dedup semantics)
# - docs/scouts/2026-07-16-taut-spectral-uuid-timestamped-shape.md
#     (Taut scout confirming LANDED carriers + zero timestamped-UUID
#      precedent in corpus; task #172)
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] (`glass
#   @uuid/spectral/time`),
# [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]] (transparency
#   inheritance through @uuid/spectral),
# [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (uuid_spectral IS the CRDT-shape
#   identity; the facet extension preserves the dedup contract),
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (~61st instance; both
#   fields LANDED; this species names the carrier the substrate
#   already implicitly used at @gestalt.annotation +
#   @spectral/signature.signature_beat),
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (uuid_spectral_time is a typed record
#   with byte-equality on the (identity, time) pair identity),
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (all action bodies `\`-obligation-
#   blocked; consumers pull the realization; Arc-1 evaluator FLOOR
#   pending),
# [[feedback-cli-subcommand-nesting-is-geometric]] (sub-species under
#   @uuid/spectral is geometric ground truth per the path-namespace
#   discipline; sibling-of-family precedent = @subject/visibility/
#   sheaf under @subject/visibility).
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/uuid/spectral/time.mirror` declares `@uuid/spectral/time`
# per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

# Sub-species under @uuid/spectral. The glass keyword (per @glass)
# marks this as a sub-prism scoped to the @uuid/spectral parent.
glass @uuid/spectral/time {
  focus  uuid_spectral_time
  project uuid_spectral_time
  split  uuid_spectral_time
  shift  uuid_spectral_time
  settle uuid_spectral_time
}

# === uuid_spectral_time — the annotation-address carrier ===
#
# The categorical product of `uuid_spectral × @time/monotonic.instant`
# with identity-projection preserving the @glass shard.id contract.
# Per docs/math/uuid/spectral-time.md §1 (composition proof, Mac Lane
# §III on categorical products).
#
# Two fields:
#
#   identity — the 128-bit uuid_spectral. @glass three-layer contract
#              intact. Content-address dedup at @mirror/store reads
#              THIS field only. The 48-bit ACTIVE prefix within
#              `identity` drives @resonance/@fate byte-comparison
#              (peer-coupling geometry unchanged; the substrate's
#              existing route_signal handle is what tournament
#              dispatch reads through).
#
#   time     — the @time/monotonic.instant facet. Full precision;
#              nanoseconds; leap-second-free. Trailing bytes when
#              serialized. Used for tie-breakers + causal ordering;
#              does NOT participate in dedup. Already composed OVER
#              by @gestalt.annotation.timestamp + @spectral/signature.
#              signature_beat.timestamp; this species lifts the
#              composition edge those consumers implicitly carried.
#
# Identity contract for content-address dedup: byte-equality on
# the `identity` field ONLY. Two uuid_spectral_time values with
# byte-equal `identity` but distinct `time` are dedup-equivalent at
# @mirror/store; storage collapses them. This is the substrate-decl
# form of "time is a facet, NOT part of identity."
#
# Identity contract for tournament ordering: byte-comparison on the
# 48-bit ACTIVE prefix of `identity`. Argsort by
# `affinity_distance(a, H_R)` IS the R4-(a) dispatch permutation.
# Per docs/math/uuid/spectral-time.md §3 (R4-affinity-by-construction
# theorem; substrate-decl form of Kuramoto-Aumann convergence at
# annotation altitude).
type uuid_spectral_time = {
  identity: uuid_spectral,
  time:     @time/monotonic.instant,
}

# === compose — the constructor ===
#
# Given a uuid_spectral (identity) and a @time/monotonic.instant
# (facet), construct the uuid_spectral_time carrier. Substrate-decl
# form of the categorical-product pair construction.
#
# The compose direction is monotone in both fields: two composes
# with byte-equal (identity, time) pairs produce byte-equal
# uuid_spectral_time. Composition-only over LANDED carriers; no new
# mechanism. Body deferred per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
compose(identity: uuid_spectral, time: @time/monotonic.instant) -> uuid_spectral_time { \ }

# === identity_of — the dedup projection ===
#
# Project the identity out of a uuid_spectral_time. Substrate-decl
# form of the categorical-product first-projection homomorphism
# preserving @mirror/store dedup equivalence (per docs/math/uuid/
# spectral-time.md §4).
#
# @mirror/store composes over this action to keep the storage layer
# unchanged: `store.put(a: uuid_spectral_time)` reduces to
# `store.put(identity_of(a))` at the dedup boundary. Two writes
# with the same content collapse regardless of time. Body deferred.
identity_of(a: uuid_spectral_time) -> uuid_spectral { \ }

# === active_prefix — the tournament-ordering handle ===
#
# Extract the 48-bit ACTIVE prefix of the identity's uuid_spectral.
# This IS the byte-comparison handle @resonance / @fate tournament
# dispatch reads through. Big-endian on ACTIVE: byte-wise sort IS
# lexicographic sort over the SpectralCoordinate<5> Fate's mycelial
# routing navigates. Range scans on the 48-bit space compose with
# byte-wise sort.
#
# Composition-only over @uuid/spectral.active (LANDED): this action
# is `active(identity_of(a))` at the substrate composition-graph
# altitude. Named at species altitude to make the tournament-
# ordering surface first-class in the annotation-address vocabulary.
# Body deferred.
active_prefix(a: uuid_spectral_time) -> ref { \ }

# === time_of — the tie-break projection ===
#
# Project the time facet out of a uuid_spectral_time. Used for
# tournament tie-breakers when two annotation addresses have byte-
# equal ACTIVE prefixes (rare at 48 bits; possible under high-
# volume peer-coupling scenarios). @fate's per-basin tie-break
# discipline composes over this action.
#
# The time facet is orthogonal to identity (per
# docs/math/uuid/spectral-time.md §4 orthogonality lemma); storage
# layer commutes with time-facet variation. Body deferred.
time_of(a: uuid_spectral_time) -> @time/monotonic.instant { \ }

# === affinity_distance — the algedonic-form gradient ===
#
# Hamming distance between the 48-bit ACTIVE prefixes of two
# uuid_spectral_time values. Returns a numeric ref (bit-count in
# the XOR of the two ACTIVE prefixes). Substrate-decl form of the
# annotation-tournament coupling weight per docs/math/uuid/
# spectral-time.md §3 (Kuramoto phase-locking reads inter-peer
# coordinate distance as coupling weight; argsort by this distance
# IS the ordering that accelerates convergence per Aumann 1976
# common-prior model).
#
# Algedonic form (per docs/math/uuid/spectral-time.md §5): byte-
# distance on ACTIVE IS the pain/pleasure gradient at address
# altitude. Small distance ↔ affinity ↔ pleasure; large distance ↔
# discord ↔ pain. @cyberpunk/algedonic composition surface can
# compose over this action for future extension; the composition
# is algedonic-form-compatible by construction. Not this arc.
#
# R4 dispatch discharge: for any reader H_R and annotation set
# A(v) = [a_1, …, a_N], the tournament permutation is
#
#   σ = argsort_i affinity_distance(a_i, H_R.address)
#
# where H_R.address IS the reader's own uuid_spectral_time carrier.
# No @fate machinery required at annotation altitude; the substrate
# carries the ordering by construction. Body deferred.
affinity_distance(a: uuid_spectral_time, b: uuid_spectral_time) -> ref { \ }

# === Bilateral predicates (dispatchable via apply_h::act) ===

# identity_contract_preserved — does the identity field satisfy the
# @glass shard.id contract?
#
# Discharges Pass iff `identity_of(a)` is a well-formed uuid_spectral
# (128 bits; route_signal + identity_signal fields both present per
# @uuid/spectral record shape; content_addressed(uuid_spectral)
# property held). Substrate-decl form: byte-level check for
# `identity=uuid-spectral-well-formed` sentinel; composes over
# @uuid/spectral's LANDED content_addressed property.
#
# Load-bearing structural claim: the facet extension does NOT
# weaken @glass's three-layer contract on the identity field. Every
# consumer that previously read shard.id: uuid_spectral can read
# identity_of(a) with identical semantics.
identity_contract_preserved(a: uuid_spectral_time) -> verdict { \ }

# time_facet_admissible — is the time field a well-formed
# @time/monotonic.instant?
#
# Discharges Pass iff `time_of(a)` is a well-formed
# @time/monotonic.instant (shift(duration) frame; non-negative
# nanoseconds by construction per settle-witness at @epistemologic/
# reality/time.mirror:71). Substrate-decl form: byte-level check
# for `time=monotonic-instant-well-formed` sentinel.
#
# Rice-safe at whole-tick altitude: reads only byte-visible state
# (the settle-witness on the duration base carrier).
time_facet_admissible(a: uuid_spectral_time) -> verdict { \ }

# dedup_ignores_time — do two carriers with byte-equal identity
# dedup to the same @mirror/store entry regardless of time?
#
# Discharges Pass iff for any (a, b) with
# `identity_of(a) == identity_of(b)` (byte-equal 128-bit prefix),
# @mirror/store treats them as dedup-equivalent (single storage
# entry). Substrate-decl form of the storage-layer invariant per
# docs/math/uuid/spectral-time.md §4 (identity_of is a projection
# homomorphism preserving @mirror/store dedup equivalence).
#
# Load-bearing structural claim: the time facet is orthogonal to
# identity at the storage boundary. @mirror/store remains unchanged
# by this species landing. Consumer cascades (Deliverable 3) can
# add the facet to annotation + signature_beat carriers without
# touching storage discipline.
dedup_ignores_time(a: uuid_spectral_time, b: uuid_spectral_time) -> verdict { \ }

# uuid_spectral_time_witnessing — the composed bilateral that
# discharges when ALL of identity_contract_preserved +
# time_facet_admissible + dedup_ignores_time hold across the
# substrate lifetime of the address.
#
# Parallel to @subject/visibility/sheaf.sheaf_witnessing and
# @gestalt.gestalt_witnessing composed-bilateral precedent. This is
# the substrate-decl form of "the annotation address is well-formed
# at every altitude: identity-side @glass contract intact; time
# facet is a valid monotonic instant; the storage layer treats the
# facet as orthogonal to identity."
uuid_spectral_time_witnessing(a: uuid_spectral_time,
                               b: uuid_spectral_time) -> verdict { \ }

# === requires predicates ===
#
# Composition obligations enforced at species altitude. Each names
# a landed cross-family carrier the substrate MUST admit for
# @uuid/spectral/time to be well-formed.

requires content_addressed(uuid_spectral)

out @uuid/spectral/time
out uuid_spectral_time
out compose
out identity_of
out active_prefix
out time_of
out affinity_distance
out identity_contract_preserved
out time_facet_admissible
out dedup_ignores_time
out uuid_spectral_time_witnessing
